      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn root equations and missing values with a small example.\n\nWe will build the method one step at a time and check each answer.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When a square-root equation contains an unknown, isolate the radical before squaring.\n\nExample: √(x+5)=7.\nSquare both sides: x+5=49.\nSo x=44.\n\nThen check in the original equation: √49=7.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
